1
00:00:48,877 --> 00:00:50,590
I...

2
00:00:51,296 --> 00:00:52,896
really...

3
00:00:54,716 --> 00:00:56,718
I like you a lot.

4
00:00:56,718 --> 00:00:58,338
Ha Na.

5
00:00:59,803 --> 00:01:01,384
[Episode 6]

6
00:01:44,855 --> 00:01:46,315
What's going on here?

7
00:01:58,571 --> 00:02:00,337
Private lesson?

8
00:02:01,241 --> 00:02:02,701
It wasn't a private lesson.

9
00:02:02,701 --> 00:02:05,620
We just ran through the script once.

10
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:08,831
What are you doing here?

11
00:02:13,926 --> 00:02:15,812
I live here now.

12
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:20,510
Guess I can read with her too.

13
00:02:20,510 --> 00:02:22,119
Right?

14
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,689
Let's go inside.

15
00:02:32,689 --> 00:02:34,132
Yeah.

16
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:06,774
Hey.

17
00:03:07,390 --> 00:03:08,787
This...

18
00:03:11,211 --> 00:03:12,413
Sorry.

19
00:03:13,062 --> 00:03:15,651
- It's okay.
- Yeah...

20
00:03:17,525 --> 00:03:18,693
Well...

21
00:03:18,693 --> 00:03:21,029
Want to go to school together tomorrow?

22
00:03:21,029 --> 00:03:22,661
What time's your class again?

23
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:26,244
Well, it starts at nine.

24
00:03:26,244 --> 00:03:27,452
Mine too.

25
00:03:27,452 --> 00:03:29,829
Then we can go together.

26
00:03:29,829 --> 00:03:32,165
Yeah, okay.

27
00:03:32,165 --> 00:03:33,434
Okay.

28
00:03:36,053 --> 00:03:37,843
<i>This clueless idiot.</i>

29
00:03:37,843 --> 00:03:40,012
<i>I'm 34. I've got experience.</i>

30
00:03:40,012 --> 00:03:43,510
<i>Let me teach you a thing or two, kid.</i>

31
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:45,678
- Jung Woo Jae.
- Yeah?

32
00:03:45,678 --> 00:03:46,888
So?

33
00:03:46,888 --> 00:03:48,515
What?

34
00:03:48,515 --> 00:03:50,642
About earlier...

35
00:03:50,642 --> 00:03:52,268
What you wanted to say to me...

36
00:03:52,268 --> 00:03:53,853
was that all?

37
00:03:53,853 --> 00:03:57,661
Yeah. I think so.

38
00:03:58,316 --> 00:04:00,235
But...

39
00:04:00,235 --> 00:04:04,426
I haven't done everything
I want to do with you.

40
00:04:06,256 --> 00:04:08,695
W-What do you want to do?

41
00:04:19,928 --> 00:04:21,798
Ha Na?

42
00:04:21,798 --> 00:04:23,303
What are you...

43
00:04:25,525 --> 00:04:26,965
<i>Ha Na...</i>

44
00:04:30,187 --> 00:04:33,518
<i>Ha Na! Ha Na!</i>

45
00:04:33,518 --> 00:04:34,966
Ha Na.

46
00:04:35,645 --> 00:04:37,477
- Ha Na?
- Yes?

47
00:04:37,477 --> 00:04:40,045
Are you okay?

48
00:04:40,692 --> 00:04:42,752
Yeah. Sure.

49
00:04:42,752 --> 00:04:44,320
Why?

50
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:47,146
You called my name.

51
00:04:51,494 --> 00:04:54,022
I'm fine.

52
00:04:54,022 --> 00:04:56,547
<i>I'm so not fine.</i>

53
00:04:57,166 --> 00:05:00,814
You're really okay?

54
00:05:01,754 --> 00:05:03,795
You feel kind of warm.

55
00:05:04,424 --> 00:05:05,916
I'm fine.

56
00:05:06,682 --> 00:05:08,767
<i>I'm disappointed in you, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

57
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,296
<i>Experienced, my ass.</i>

58
00:05:10,296 --> 00:05:12,789
<i>Why am I so nervous?</i>

59
00:05:13,734 --> 00:05:16,227
- Want me to get you some medicine?
- No!

60
00:05:16,227 --> 00:05:19,543
I'm really fine.

61
00:05:20,273 --> 00:05:21,274
Tell me if you feel sick.

62
00:05:21,274 --> 00:05:23,151
We can go to the ER, okay?

63
00:05:23,151 --> 00:05:24,908
Yeah.

64
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:26,253
Okay.

65
00:05:27,097 --> 00:05:28,615
See you tomorrow.

66
00:05:28,615 --> 00:05:30,783
Yeah.

67
00:05:30,783 --> 00:05:34,495
It's late. Get some rest.

68
00:05:34,495 --> 00:05:36,623
Then... I'm off.

69
00:05:36,623 --> 00:05:37,819
Okay.

70
00:05:38,458 --> 00:05:39,778
Yeah.

71
00:05:40,835 --> 00:05:42,129
Yeah.

72
00:05:42,129 --> 00:05:44,213
- Okay.
- Okay.

73
00:05:44,213 --> 00:05:45,417
Yeah...

74
00:05:46,341 --> 00:05:48,699
- Nine...
- Yeah.

75
00:05:49,344 --> 00:05:50,686
Yeah.

76
00:06:35,056 --> 00:06:37,250
Come on, Yoon Ha Na.

77
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:40,369
I'm 34! Why is this so hard?

78
00:06:47,735 --> 00:06:51,328
<i>I really like you.</i>

79
00:06:53,141 --> 00:06:54,659
<i>I...</i>

80
00:06:54,659 --> 00:06:56,319
<i>really...</i>

81
00:06:57,286 --> 00:06:59,388
<i>I like you a lot.</i>

82
00:07:03,776 --> 00:07:05,294
Oh my...

83
00:07:05,294 --> 00:07:09,048
It's because he is too cute and too cool.

84
00:07:09,048 --> 00:07:10,314
That's all it is.

85
00:07:10,314 --> 00:07:12,677
It's his fault.

86
00:07:12,677 --> 00:07:14,721
And what was with that move?

87
00:07:14,721 --> 00:07:17,239
Seriously, Jung Woo Jae...

88
00:07:17,239 --> 00:07:18,719
Beats me.

89
00:07:21,894 --> 00:07:25,538
And what's with Lee Hyeong Won?

90
00:07:25,538 --> 00:07:27,650
Taking Woo Jae's national team spot
wasn't enough?

91
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:30,323
Why does he keep showing up
and acting like we're close?

92
00:07:30,323 --> 00:07:32,822
What if he takes the audition from him too...

93
00:07:32,822 --> 00:07:33,823
No.

94
00:07:33,823 --> 00:07:35,863
Absolutely not.

95
00:07:39,149 --> 00:07:40,621
[Beast]

96
00:07:40,621 --> 00:07:42,874
<i>The phone you have called is turned off.</i>

97
00:07:42,874 --> 00:07:44,042
<i>You'll be sent to voicemail...</i>

98
00:07:44,042 --> 00:07:45,334
What?

99
00:07:45,334 --> 00:07:47,249
Why is his phone off?

100
00:07:48,337 --> 00:07:50,289
Seriously.

101
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,761
[Hanjin Chicken]

102
00:07:54,761 --> 00:07:56,168
Let's drink.

103
00:07:57,614 --> 00:07:59,108
What's this?

104
00:08:01,559 --> 00:08:02,560
It's crispy.

105
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:04,896
Chewy too. This is really good.

106
00:08:04,896 --> 00:08:07,857
It's not that harsh,
artificial capsaicin stuff.

107
00:08:07,857 --> 00:08:11,506
It's that subtle heat
from Cheongyang peppers...

108
00:08:12,361 --> 00:08:14,296
This is addictive.

109
00:08:14,953 --> 00:08:16,824
Hey, look.

110
00:08:16,824 --> 00:08:19,285
Stop eating and listen.

111
00:08:19,285 --> 00:08:21,454
Ever since Ha Na started school here,

112
00:08:21,454 --> 00:08:25,583
she's been the lead in every Yang Jun Mo film.

113
00:08:25,583 --> 00:08:27,460
And everything he made with Ha Na

114
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:29,754
was an official selection at Mise-en-scène.

115
00:08:29,754 --> 00:08:32,673
Makers Film went crazy for them too.

116
00:08:32,673 --> 00:08:37,059
I don't know if it was some lovers' quarrel,

117
00:08:37,059 --> 00:08:39,013
but there was one time...

118
00:08:39,013 --> 00:08:41,641
when Ha Na turned down his film.

119
00:08:41,641 --> 00:08:44,644
Know what happened to it?

120
00:08:44,644 --> 00:08:45,817
What was it called again?

121
00:08:45,817 --> 00:08:48,022
See? You can't even remember.

122
00:08:48,022 --> 00:08:51,067
That's why Yang Jun Mo can't let her go.

123
00:08:51,067 --> 00:08:54,654
Why? Because without Ha Na,
it's not a Yang Jun Mo film.

124
00:08:54,654 --> 00:08:57,281
How could he not fall for her?

125
00:08:57,281 --> 00:08:59,539
- I would too...
- How did you even get there?

126
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:01,452
Exactly.

127
00:09:01,452 --> 00:09:04,288
Yeah. Guess he would fall for her.

128
00:09:04,288 --> 00:09:06,290
So even though every character was different...

129
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:08,709
so Ha Na was always the lead.

130
00:09:08,709 --> 00:09:12,886
That's why directing majors
don't even hit on her.

131
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:16,038
Everyone assumes Ha Na is Jun Mo's.

132
00:09:16,038 --> 00:09:18,305
The more I think about it,
the more it pisses me off.

133
00:09:18,305 --> 00:09:19,929
Greedy bastard.

134
00:09:19,929 --> 00:09:22,056
Am I wrong?

135
00:09:22,056 --> 00:09:25,461
I wonder how far those two have gone.

136
00:09:25,461 --> 00:09:27,186
Seriously.

137
00:09:27,186 --> 00:09:28,809
No way.

138
00:09:30,324 --> 00:09:31,530
Wait.

139
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:34,902
I think I heard a rumor like that once.

140
00:09:34,902 --> 00:09:36,571
Wow, that explains it.

141
00:09:36,571 --> 00:09:39,077
No way.

142
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:41,868
You just ruined my drink.

143
00:09:41,868 --> 00:09:43,180
I'll take it.

144
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:44,877
You stormed out too.

145
00:09:44,877 --> 00:09:46,336
You know something, huh?

146
00:09:46,336 --> 00:09:47,337
What?

147
00:09:47,337 --> 00:09:48,374
What is it?

148
00:09:48,374 --> 00:09:49,667
Come on, tell us.

149
00:09:49,667 --> 00:09:52,170
I lost my temper once,

150
00:09:52,170 --> 00:09:54,932
and now you're lumping me in with you?

151
00:09:54,932 --> 00:09:57,055
This is so damn annoying.

152
00:09:57,675 --> 00:09:59,093
You're talking about me?

153
00:09:59,093 --> 00:10:01,345
- Bi Gyeong.
- Yes?

154
00:10:01,345 --> 00:10:05,266
Know why Ha Na gets cast
in all those different roles?

155
00:10:05,266 --> 00:10:07,185
Because she can pull them all off.

156
00:10:07,185 --> 00:10:10,020
She actually becomes the character.

157
00:10:11,105 --> 00:10:13,107
While you're sitting here trashing her,

158
00:10:13,107 --> 00:10:15,074
she's probably reading her script.

159
00:10:15,074 --> 00:10:17,069
- Hey...
- What?

160
00:10:17,069 --> 00:10:19,054
That hurt?

161
00:10:19,675 --> 00:10:23,278
Ha Na would be pretty pissed if she saw this.

162
00:10:23,278 --> 00:10:24,887
You're actors too,

163
00:10:24,887 --> 00:10:28,838
yet you're acting as if she got cast
for something besides talent.

164
00:10:28,838 --> 00:10:30,291
And you're her classmate.

165
00:10:30,291 --> 00:10:31,626
So?

166
00:10:31,626 --> 00:10:33,294
What do you get out of this?

167
00:10:33,294 --> 00:10:39,425
Does putting her down change the fact
that you're not as good as she is?

168
00:10:39,425 --> 00:10:40,557
Feel better now?

169
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:42,261
Seo Ye Rang.

170
00:10:42,261 --> 00:10:44,124
Seo Ye Rang.

171
00:10:44,124 --> 00:10:45,395
That's enough.

172
00:10:45,395 --> 00:10:47,934
You're the one who looks pathetic right now.
You know that?

173
00:10:47,934 --> 00:10:49,101
What?

174
00:10:49,101 --> 00:10:52,236
Your script didn't pass review,
so it never got made.

175
00:10:52,236 --> 00:10:55,052
Jun Mo's did and yours didn't.

176
00:10:55,052 --> 00:10:56,484
Jealous?

177
00:10:56,484 --> 00:11:02,198
So you're writing some story about
a director and actress having a dirty affair?

178
00:11:02,198 --> 00:11:03,863
And it doesn't even make any sense.

179
00:11:03,863 --> 00:11:06,490
- You won't quit, will you?
- At least...

180
00:11:07,376 --> 00:11:10,706
Jun Mo doesn't screw around
when it comes to his work.

181
00:11:10,706 --> 00:11:13,876
That's why we're all dying
to get into one of his shorts.

182
00:11:13,876 --> 00:11:15,839
You all know that.

183
00:11:21,014 --> 00:11:22,593
What we're trying to do

184
00:11:22,593 --> 00:11:25,596
is tell stories about people's hearts.

185
00:11:25,596 --> 00:11:27,932
But with hearts this ugly,

186
00:11:27,932 --> 00:11:32,561
how are we supposed to move anyone
with our films?

187
00:11:32,561 --> 00:11:35,075
Can we stop being so pathetic?

188
00:11:36,107 --> 00:11:38,073
Lie down with dogs, wake up with fleas.

189
00:11:38,073 --> 00:11:39,146
Remember that.

190
00:11:39,146 --> 00:11:40,582
Yes.

191
00:11:40,582 --> 00:11:42,080
What's with her?

192
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:43,622
Hey!

193
00:11:44,413 --> 00:11:47,569
Seo Ye Rang, you're still awesome.

194
00:11:55,883 --> 00:11:57,918
Bitter!

195
00:11:59,922 --> 00:12:02,284
Oh, I'm so drunk...

196
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:06,280
No, no.

197
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:07,680
Pull yourself together.

198
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,540
Get it together.

199
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:22,242
You're that psycho from before.

200
00:12:23,821 --> 00:12:26,435
Eat something. You'll wreck your stomach.

201
00:12:28,159 --> 00:12:31,252
I don't take food from suspicious people.

202
00:12:36,366 --> 00:12:38,019
Fair.

203
00:12:43,632 --> 00:12:45,509
Why are you sitting down?

204
00:12:45,509 --> 00:12:47,649
Because I want to stay with you.

205
00:12:48,797 --> 00:12:50,585
Are you kidding me?

206
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:58,333
Look closely.

207
00:13:02,568 --> 00:13:04,403
What do you think?

208
00:13:04,403 --> 00:13:07,907
Still can't tell?

209
00:13:07,907 --> 00:13:11,427
Nothing? Your heart's not racing?

210
00:13:19,710 --> 00:13:21,712
I have really high standards.

211
00:13:21,712 --> 00:13:24,940
Most people don't do a thing for me.

212
00:13:25,758 --> 00:13:28,312
I'm seriously drunk.

213
00:13:30,130 --> 00:13:32,056
What is this?

214
00:13:36,185 --> 00:13:37,958
<i>Boss.</i>

215
00:13:37,958 --> 00:13:38,985
<i>Hi.</i>

216
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:40,856
<i>Babe!</i>

217
00:13:40,856 --> 00:13:43,569
<i>How'd you get here?</i>

218
00:13:45,312 --> 00:13:47,238
<i>- You really are something...
- What?</i>

219
00:13:47,238 --> 00:13:49,361
<i>You never get tired of me, do you?</i>

220
00:13:49,361 --> 00:13:50,703
<i>Never.</i>

221
00:13:50,703 --> 00:13:53,160
<i>Every time I see you,
I fall for you all over again.</i>

222
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:55,746
<i>14 years and counting.</i>

223
00:13:55,746 --> 00:13:56,872
<i>Am I that irresistible?</i>

224
00:13:56,872 --> 00:14:00,099
<i>Of course.
You think I would choose just anyone?</i>

225
00:14:03,113 --> 00:14:04,786
<i>Oh, please.</i>

226
00:14:05,667 --> 00:14:09,969
<i>I've only ever lived in a world where
I thought falling for me was a given.</i>

227
00:14:09,969 --> 00:14:13,167
<i>I never knew a world
where you didn't fall for me</i>

228
00:14:13,167 --> 00:14:15,869
<i>could feel so strange...</i>

229
00:14:15,869 --> 00:14:17,852
And sad.

230
00:14:19,186 --> 00:14:21,119
What are you talking about?

231
00:14:24,108 --> 00:14:26,742
You're handsome, though.

232
00:14:26,742 --> 00:14:27,934
Right?

233
00:14:27,934 --> 00:14:30,939
Give it time. Your heart will start racing.

234
00:14:30,939 --> 00:14:32,692
When it does, you have to tell me.

235
00:14:32,692 --> 00:14:34,928
That you've fallen for me. Promise!

236
00:14:34,928 --> 00:14:36,260
What?

237
00:14:39,206 --> 00:14:42,196
Aren't you going home? It's late.

238
00:14:42,196 --> 00:14:43,848
Hands off.

239
00:14:44,462 --> 00:14:46,454
I am.

240
00:15:00,811 --> 00:15:02,892
Don't follow me.

241
00:15:23,523 --> 00:15:25,586
[Happy Home]

242
00:15:25,586 --> 00:15:29,134
Look at me, Boss.

243
00:15:29,757 --> 00:15:31,406
It's me.

244
00:15:32,384 --> 00:15:33,594
Darn it.

245
00:15:33,594 --> 00:15:36,019
Hey! Why didn't you answer yesterday?

246
00:15:36,019 --> 00:15:37,688
Don't you knock?

247
00:15:37,688 --> 00:15:39,225
Why would I?

248
00:15:39,225 --> 00:15:40,651
You...

249
00:15:44,319 --> 00:15:46,941
- Do you know Lee Hyeong Won?
- What?

250
00:15:46,941 --> 00:15:49,057
Who's that now?

251
00:15:52,071 --> 00:15:53,759
Oh, Lee Hyeong Won!

252
00:15:54,423 --> 00:15:55,741
When you were in my body...

253
00:15:55,741 --> 00:15:58,559
that judo thug you competed against.

254
00:16:01,929 --> 00:16:04,448
[That Summer, Us]

255
00:16:59,410 --> 00:17:01,286
One for me...

256
00:17:05,394 --> 00:17:07,229
Fried eggs! Looks good.

257
00:17:07,229 --> 00:17:08,314
Want me to flip them?

258
00:17:08,314 --> 00:17:09,398
- Want to try?
- Yeah.

259
00:17:09,398 --> 00:17:10,892
Careful.

260
00:17:10,892 --> 00:17:13,067
Thanks. Take care.

261
00:17:18,389 --> 00:17:22,952
What a world. The owner delivers
sundae-guk in an earthenware pot.

262
00:17:24,448 --> 00:17:25,654
Look at this.

263
00:17:25,654 --> 00:17:28,702
Nothing beats sundae-guk in an earthenware pot.

264
00:17:28,702 --> 00:17:31,337
Compared to soup in a disposable plastic bowl,

265
00:17:31,337 --> 00:17:33,842
this is on another level.

266
00:17:36,175 --> 00:17:37,571
Oh, man.

267
00:17:38,563 --> 00:17:39,784
But...

268
00:17:39,784 --> 00:17:43,983
Do places actually deliver
sundae-guk in plastic containers?

269
00:17:44,675 --> 00:17:47,795
I don't know either.

270
00:18:01,206 --> 00:18:02,572
Hey.

271
00:18:17,216 --> 00:18:20,440
That diet says you haven't quit judo.

272
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:23,207
Hey, why are you here?

273
00:18:23,207 --> 00:18:24,842
Did you screw up?

274
00:18:25,432 --> 00:18:26,953
Wait...

275
00:18:27,976 --> 00:18:29,744
Did you get cut?

276
00:18:30,441 --> 00:18:33,856
I didn't screw up, and I didn't get kicked off.

277
00:18:35,109 --> 00:18:36,533
That doesn't make sense.

278
00:18:36,533 --> 00:18:39,196
A coach just lets his athlete leave like this?

279
00:18:39,196 --> 00:18:41,790
No supervision? Just lets you roam free?

280
00:18:41,790 --> 00:18:44,294
No way.

281
00:18:45,162 --> 00:18:47,121
It's not neglect. It's trust.

282
00:18:47,121 --> 00:18:50,415
Coaches micromanage guys
who can't deliver on the mat.

283
00:18:51,053 --> 00:18:54,753
I guess medalists really do get
special treatment.

284
00:18:54,753 --> 00:18:56,964
Look at that confidence.

285
00:18:56,964 --> 00:18:59,717
Lee Hyeong Won, you've grown up.

286
00:18:59,717 --> 00:19:03,915
I'm so proud of you.

287
00:19:07,175 --> 00:19:10,880
But why are you auditioning for a short film?

288
00:19:13,153 --> 00:19:14,412
What?

289
00:19:15,531 --> 00:19:17,358
You little...

290
00:19:17,358 --> 00:19:18,885
Hey.

291
00:19:18,885 --> 00:19:20,571
What's your dream?

292
00:19:21,989 --> 00:19:25,492
I asked you what your dream is, punk.

293
00:19:25,492 --> 00:19:26,493
Get lost.

294
00:19:26,493 --> 00:19:27,745
<i>Where are you going?</i>

295
00:19:27,745 --> 00:19:29,288
<i>Get lost.</i>

296
00:19:29,288 --> 00:19:32,916
Damn, always telling me to get lost.

297
00:19:32,916 --> 00:19:34,918
You're on the national team, idiot.

298
00:19:34,918 --> 00:19:38,345
You represent Korea, remember?

299
00:19:38,345 --> 00:19:39,423
Is this really the time?

300
00:19:39,423 --> 00:19:41,216
Is this what you should be doing right now?

301
00:19:41,216 --> 00:19:44,261
At a time like this, a short film audition?

302
00:19:44,261 --> 00:19:46,294
Unbelievable.

303
00:19:46,294 --> 00:19:48,334
Are you that out of touch?

304
00:19:48,334 --> 00:19:50,321
<i>Are you that out of touch?</i>

305
00:19:54,396 --> 00:19:55,814
Choose.

306
00:19:55,814 --> 00:19:57,357
You want to be a national team medalist?

307
00:19:57,357 --> 00:20:00,347
Or waste your time elsewhere
and end up a miserable twat?

308
00:20:00,347 --> 00:20:01,713
<i>Choose.</i>

309
00:20:01,713 --> 00:20:05,123
<i>Be a judo player, or end up a miserable twat.</i>

310
00:20:18,003 --> 00:20:21,477
Was I too harsh?

311
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:27,930
He didn't even finish his food...

312
00:20:31,391 --> 00:20:32,957
Seo Ye Rang.

313
00:20:34,228 --> 00:20:37,409
How did you pull off all this on this budget?

314
00:20:37,409 --> 00:20:39,792
I'm a producer. It's what I do.

315
00:20:40,859 --> 00:20:44,029
You secured Haesol City
as our filming location,

316
00:20:44,029 --> 00:20:46,698
and Ha Na's family home as our base camp.

317
00:20:46,698 --> 00:20:49,243
That freed up some room in the budget.

318
00:20:49,243 --> 00:20:54,206
So stop worrying about everything else
and focus on directing.

319
00:20:54,206 --> 00:20:56,166
I can count on you, Ye Rang.

320
00:20:56,166 --> 00:20:57,420
Thanks.

321
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:59,078
Don't mention it.

322
00:21:01,213 --> 00:21:03,340
After getting that private coaching,

323
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:05,801
I'd better nail this audition.

324
00:21:05,801 --> 00:21:09,596
No. Don't think about doing well. Just do it.

325
00:21:09,596 --> 00:21:12,413
How am I supposed to "just do it?"

326
00:21:15,185 --> 00:21:17,688
<i>Just pretend they're all me.</i>

327
00:21:17,688 --> 00:21:19,682
<i>Everyone out there.</i>

328
00:21:21,024 --> 00:21:23,652
Just pretend they're all me.

329
00:21:23,652 --> 00:21:25,618
Everyone in there.

330
00:21:27,614 --> 00:21:28,876
Okay.

331
00:21:32,417 --> 00:21:33,854
Ha Na!

332
00:21:50,929 --> 00:21:52,410
You okay?

333
00:21:54,349 --> 00:21:57,019
Oh, Jung Woo Jae.

334
00:21:57,019 --> 00:21:58,478
That was bold.

335
00:21:58,478 --> 00:22:02,181
You really startled me.

336
00:22:02,181 --> 00:22:03,776
Cute.

337
00:22:05,952 --> 00:22:07,405
Shall we go?

338
00:22:18,118 --> 00:22:19,230
My treat.

339
00:22:19,230 --> 00:22:21,514
- What do you want?
- Anything.

340
00:22:23,490 --> 00:22:24,992
Wait.

341
00:22:25,619 --> 00:22:28,298
Are those two together?

342
00:22:32,554 --> 00:22:34,073
Looks like it.

343
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:37,142
I had no idea...

344
00:22:37,142 --> 00:22:41,063
Look at you, watching them like a hawk.
Such a director.

345
00:22:41,063 --> 00:22:43,023
Was I?

346
00:22:43,023 --> 00:22:44,033
Yeah.

347
00:22:44,033 --> 00:22:45,505
I thought the audition had already started.

348
00:22:45,505 --> 00:22:47,019
Come on.

349
00:22:47,753 --> 00:22:49,442
Let's go.

350
00:23:04,211 --> 00:23:07,368
Isn't that Ye Rang's car?

351
00:23:07,368 --> 00:23:10,300
Who the hell is that getting out of her car?

352
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:11,679
Boss!

353
00:23:19,525 --> 00:23:21,964
Why do you keep calling me "Boss?"

354
00:23:24,606 --> 00:23:26,168
Give me your number!

355
00:23:30,123 --> 00:23:31,736
Let's go.

356
00:23:35,909 --> 00:23:38,661
- Come on.
- Yeah, coming.

357
00:23:41,456 --> 00:23:45,505
I look handsome today... Right?

358
00:23:46,378 --> 00:23:47,782
Did her type...

359
00:23:48,886 --> 00:23:50,514
change?

360
00:23:58,483 --> 00:24:00,417
<i>- Get lost.
- Where are you going?</i>

361
00:24:00,417 --> 00:24:01,643
<i>It's not over for you yet.</i>

362
00:24:01,643 --> 00:24:02,923
<i>There's a repechage.</i>

363
00:24:02,923 --> 00:24:06,227
<i>Damn, always telling me to get lost.</i>

364
00:24:07,065 --> 00:24:08,275
<i>Choose.</i>

365
00:24:08,275 --> 00:24:09,943
<i>You want to be a national team medalist?</i>

366
00:24:09,943 --> 00:24:12,446
<i>Or waste your time elsewhere
and end up a miserable twat?</i>

367
00:24:12,446 --> 00:24:13,527
<i>Choose.</i>

368
00:24:13,527 --> 00:24:16,931
<i>Be a judo player, or end up a miserable twat.</i>

369
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:39,814
[That Summer, Us]

370
00:24:56,246 --> 00:24:58,444
Private lessons behind my back?

371
00:24:59,930 --> 00:25:01,606
Feeling threatened, huh?

372
00:25:04,503 --> 00:25:06,384
What?

373
00:25:06,384 --> 00:25:10,710
Why do you keep coming at me nonstop?

374
00:25:10,710 --> 00:25:12,703
And now Ha Na too.

375
00:25:18,435 --> 00:25:22,537
You think I only made the national team
because you got hurt, right?

376
00:25:23,183 --> 00:25:25,901
You know why I made it?

377
00:25:25,901 --> 00:25:27,738
I wanted it more.

378
00:25:28,683 --> 00:25:31,101
More than you did.

379
00:25:33,944 --> 00:25:35,695
Let's say that's true.

380
00:25:35,695 --> 00:25:37,364
Do whatever you want to me.

381
00:25:37,364 --> 00:25:38,506
But...

382
00:25:38,506 --> 00:25:40,158
leave Ha Na alone.

383
00:25:40,158 --> 00:25:42,024
I'm serious.

384
00:25:42,904 --> 00:25:45,043
That's your problem.

385
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:49,856
Turns out, it wasn't just the medal
that I wanted to take from you.

386
00:25:49,856 --> 00:25:52,368
I want her just as badly.

387
00:26:07,310 --> 00:26:08,978
Wait.

388
00:26:12,524 --> 00:26:15,517
Okay, let's do this.

389
00:26:15,517 --> 00:26:20,240
I assume you all know my résumé.

390
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,575
All right!

391
00:26:21,575 --> 00:26:24,119
The dish you're about to make

392
00:26:24,119 --> 00:26:27,542
is the one dessert you'd put out into the world

393
00:26:27,542 --> 00:26:30,888
with your hotel's name on it.

394
00:26:30,888 --> 00:26:33,044
What matters is...

395
00:26:33,044 --> 00:26:35,422
taste, visuals, commercial appeal.

396
00:26:35,422 --> 00:26:37,617
Flavor, presentation, marketability!

397
00:26:37,617 --> 00:26:41,661
Not one of those
can fall short of my strict standards.

398
00:26:41,661 --> 00:26:45,974
Only one plate survives.

399
00:26:45,974 --> 00:26:49,060
Everything else goes in the trash.

400
00:26:49,060 --> 00:26:51,938
You know what I'm saying, right?

401
00:26:51,938 --> 00:26:57,285
- You get one shot...
<i>- An apron instead of a judo uniform.</i>

402
00:26:57,285 --> 00:26:59,578
Ready, go!

403
00:26:59,578 --> 00:27:00,954
Start cooking!

404
00:27:00,954 --> 00:27:04,333
<i>I used to throw people. Now I'm pounding dough?</i>

405
00:27:04,333 --> 00:27:05,823
No way...

406
00:27:08,670 --> 00:27:10,450
Terrible!

407
00:27:11,041 --> 00:27:12,834
Are you crazy?

408
00:27:12,834 --> 00:27:13,835
Sorry?

409
00:27:13,835 --> 00:27:16,241
No time! Move!

410
00:27:17,172 --> 00:27:18,340
Focus!

411
00:27:18,340 --> 00:27:19,721
Just focus!

412
00:27:19,721 --> 00:27:21,181
Okay...

413
00:27:21,181 --> 00:27:25,657
Mom was right. I can't blow my tuition
and get smacked by her too.

414
00:27:25,657 --> 00:27:27,078
Let's do this.

415
00:27:27,078 --> 00:27:28,975
Cooking is your life!

416
00:27:28,975 --> 00:27:32,861
Give it everything you've got!

417
00:27:38,276 --> 00:27:40,916
- Look at the food!
- Oh, right.

418
00:27:40,916 --> 00:27:42,388
Look!

419
00:27:42,388 --> 00:27:43,894
Hey! You...

420
00:27:59,256 --> 00:28:00,818
<i>This is it.</i>

421
00:28:37,830 --> 00:28:39,729
Interesting.

422
00:28:48,564 --> 00:28:50,312
Shit...

423
00:28:50,312 --> 00:28:52,616
You are a loser!

424
00:29:04,779 --> 00:29:06,114
Is this food?

425
00:29:06,114 --> 00:29:07,782
Is this food?

426
00:29:07,782 --> 00:29:11,655
I can't stop myself! So pissed off!

427
00:29:27,302 --> 00:29:28,595
What's this?

428
00:29:28,595 --> 00:29:30,613
It's Dujjonku.

429
00:29:31,353 --> 00:29:32,707
"Du..." What?

430
00:29:32,707 --> 00:29:34,476
Dubai Chewy Cookie.

431
00:29:34,476 --> 00:29:36,186
Dujjonku.

432
00:29:36,186 --> 00:29:38,980
"Dujjonku..."

433
00:29:38,980 --> 00:29:42,503
Pick it up and take a bite.

434
00:29:43,710 --> 00:29:45,445
With my bare hands?

435
00:29:45,445 --> 00:29:46,738
Yes.

436
00:29:46,738 --> 00:29:48,500
Impossible.

437
00:29:52,869 --> 00:29:54,808
Oh, the smell.

438
00:30:06,424 --> 00:30:09,022
<i>With every bite, it bursts open,</i>

439
00:30:09,022 --> 00:30:12,806
<i>revealing that pale green pistachio inside.</i>

440
00:30:12,806 --> 00:30:15,141
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

441
00:30:15,141 --> 00:30:17,644
<i>And with every bite, that crunch...</i>

442
00:30:17,644 --> 00:30:19,938
<i>This is incredible!</i>

443
00:30:19,938 --> 00:30:22,732
<i>Oh, fantastic!</i>

444
00:30:22,732 --> 00:30:24,318
<i>And while you're eating it...</i>

445
00:30:24,318 --> 00:30:29,197
<i>this innovative texture
makes you want to pay more for it.</i>

446
00:30:29,197 --> 00:30:31,329
<i>That's got serious commercial potential!</i>

447
00:30:31,329 --> 00:30:33,137
<i>Very good!</i>

448
00:30:39,874 --> 00:30:40,883
Amazing!

449
00:30:40,883 --> 00:30:43,356
Bravo! Mamma mia!

450
00:30:43,356 --> 00:30:45,991
It tastes like ice cream.

451
00:30:47,006 --> 00:30:49,551
This is a dessert revolution.

452
00:30:49,551 --> 00:30:52,198
Mr. Yoon Ha Ru.

453
00:30:52,935 --> 00:30:54,622
Thank you.

454
00:30:54,622 --> 00:30:56,249
Let's give him a hand!

455
00:30:56,249 --> 00:30:57,629
Applause!

456
00:30:58,468 --> 00:30:59,923
You're the best!

457
00:31:08,649 --> 00:31:12,490
Actually, this is for someone.

458
00:31:12,490 --> 00:31:13,739
Okay.

459
00:31:14,449 --> 00:31:15,934
I don't care.

460
00:31:21,809 --> 00:31:23,602
[Auditions for the male lead]

461
00:31:25,222 --> 00:31:26,475
[That Summer, Us]

462
00:31:27,964 --> 00:31:30,467
Gang Ho got So Hee to safety,

463
00:31:30,467 --> 00:31:33,052
and now he has to leave to fight again.

464
00:31:33,052 --> 00:31:34,471
Improvise the dialogue.

465
00:31:34,471 --> 00:31:36,639
Say your final goodbye to So Hee.

466
00:31:36,639 --> 00:31:37,827
Okay.

467
00:31:53,705 --> 00:31:55,998
I'll kill them all.

468
00:31:57,118 --> 00:31:59,329
Anyone who hurts you...

469
00:31:59,329 --> 00:32:02,697
I won't leave a single one alive.

470
00:32:02,697 --> 00:32:04,226
Just trust me.

471
00:32:11,925 --> 00:32:13,384
I can do better.

472
00:32:13,384 --> 00:32:15,067
What are you talking about?

473
00:32:17,180 --> 00:32:19,015
Isn't that good enough?

474
00:32:19,015 --> 00:32:20,436
Yeah?

475
00:32:34,392 --> 00:32:35,624
Go ahead and start.

476
00:32:35,624 --> 00:32:36,894
Okay.

477
00:32:40,537 --> 00:32:43,314
<i>Just pretend they're all me.</i>

478
00:32:43,314 --> 00:32:45,022
<i>Everyone in there.</i>

479
00:33:15,154 --> 00:33:17,434
No need to be scared.

480
00:33:18,832 --> 00:33:21,119
If you wait for me,

481
00:33:21,119 --> 00:33:23,538
I'll come back. I promise.

482
00:33:23,538 --> 00:33:25,957
Even if you're in the middle of hell,

483
00:33:25,957 --> 00:33:29,278
I'll protect you.

484
00:33:31,261 --> 00:33:33,714
Just trust me, okay?

485
00:34:04,537 --> 00:34:06,873
So who are you picking?

486
00:34:06,873 --> 00:34:10,001
You need to decide, Jun Mo.

487
00:34:10,001 --> 00:34:12,337
It comes down to balance.

488
00:34:12,337 --> 00:34:13,880
If buzz is 90,

489
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:15,840
acting only needs to be 10 to get funded.

490
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:19,177
What if acting is 90 and buzz is 10?

491
00:34:19,177 --> 00:34:20,637
That's a tough sell.

492
00:34:20,637 --> 00:34:22,138
Being famous...

493
00:34:22,138 --> 00:34:25,099
is a lot more power than you think.

494
00:34:25,099 --> 00:34:27,933
We're out of time.

495
00:34:28,603 --> 00:34:30,188
Any objections?

496
00:34:30,188 --> 00:34:31,803
I do.

497
00:34:32,440 --> 00:34:37,070
You all saw a total rookie
change the whole room.

498
00:34:37,070 --> 00:34:40,406
And we're just throwing away
that kind of buzz potential?

499
00:34:40,406 --> 00:34:42,768
I agree with that.

500
00:34:42,768 --> 00:34:45,671
Yeah, but...

501
00:34:45,671 --> 00:34:47,955
Walking away from buzz
that dropped right into our laps...

502
00:34:47,955 --> 00:34:49,378
Darn it...

503
00:34:49,378 --> 00:34:51,376
Almost impossible.

504
00:34:51,376 --> 00:34:53,152
Exactly.

505
00:34:54,045 --> 00:34:56,172
All right.

506
00:34:56,172 --> 00:34:57,840
Why are we making this film?

507
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:59,258
Why?

508
00:34:59,258 --> 00:35:00,760
So people will watch it.

509
00:35:00,760 --> 00:35:03,513
Who would audiences rather see as Gang Ho?

510
00:35:03,513 --> 00:35:06,391
National team star Lee Hyeong Won?

511
00:35:06,391 --> 00:35:09,644
Or some nobody named Jung Woo Jae?

512
00:35:09,644 --> 00:35:12,154
Isn't the answer obvious?

513
00:35:12,154 --> 00:35:14,257
Right. Fame is always a plus.

514
00:35:14,257 --> 00:35:16,009
Exactly!

515
00:35:19,404 --> 00:35:21,126
I'll make the call.

516
00:35:30,049 --> 00:35:32,956
<i>The role of Gang Ho...</i>

517
00:35:34,961 --> 00:35:37,130
<i>goes to Hyeong Won.</i>

518
00:35:37,130 --> 00:35:40,469
<i>Woo Jae, thank you for all your hard work.</i>

519
00:36:00,987 --> 00:36:03,740
This can't be happening.

520
00:36:03,740 --> 00:36:05,831
This is driving me crazy.

521
00:36:10,504 --> 00:36:12,999
We're in this together now,
so let's make it work.

522
00:36:12,999 --> 00:36:15,251
I'll do my best.

523
00:36:15,251 --> 00:36:16,711
Hey, national team!

524
00:36:16,711 --> 00:36:18,463
Your right side really is your good side.

525
00:36:18,463 --> 00:36:21,064
- Yeah.
- She brought the camcorder?

526
00:36:21,983 --> 00:36:23,468
Why'd you take that out?

527
00:36:23,468 --> 00:36:24,886
Isn't that Ha Na's bag?

528
00:36:24,886 --> 00:36:28,473
We're classmates.
What's the big deal if I touch it?

529
00:36:28,473 --> 00:36:32,602
On the historic day
Hyeong Won landed the role...

530
00:36:32,602 --> 00:36:35,772
let's get it on camera.

531
00:36:35,772 --> 00:36:37,106
Yoon Ha Na.

532
00:36:37,106 --> 00:36:38,232
Ha Na.

533
00:36:38,232 --> 00:36:40,390
Say hello to your new co-star.

534
00:36:40,390 --> 00:36:41,567
Okay.

535
00:36:41,567 --> 00:36:43,078
Congrats. Let's do a good job.

536
00:36:43,078 --> 00:36:44,300
Yeah.

537
00:36:48,786 --> 00:36:50,745
Ha Na, why won't this turn on?

538
00:36:50,745 --> 00:36:51,954
Maybe it's broken.

539
00:36:51,954 --> 00:36:53,804
Hey! Why are you touching...

540
00:37:06,018 --> 00:37:08,672
Hey, are you okay?

541
00:37:10,306 --> 00:37:11,417
Come on.

542
00:37:11,417 --> 00:37:14,886
Why make such a big deal out of it?

543
00:37:15,531 --> 00:37:17,509
"A big deal?"

544
00:37:17,509 --> 00:37:21,859
It didn't even work to begin with.

545
00:37:21,859 --> 00:37:25,677
Now you're making me
look like some kind of jerk.

546
00:37:26,767 --> 00:37:28,658
Shin Bi Gyeong.

547
00:37:28,658 --> 00:37:30,407
Apologize.

548
00:37:30,993 --> 00:37:33,098
- What?
- So being classmates...

549
00:37:33,098 --> 00:37:35,873
means you can touch her stuff,

550
00:37:35,873 --> 00:37:38,835
but she can't tell you to stop?

551
00:37:38,835 --> 00:37:41,587
You should feel embarrassed.

552
00:37:41,587 --> 00:37:44,651
So apologize.

553
00:37:48,980 --> 00:37:52,232
Sorry, Yoon Ha Na.

554
00:37:54,439 --> 00:37:56,887
I'll head out first.

555
00:37:57,774 --> 00:37:59,745
Ha Na!

556
00:38:02,817 --> 00:38:04,323
Seriously...

557
00:38:07,539 --> 00:38:10,238
What's taking her so long?

558
00:38:14,078 --> 00:38:15,744
Oh, good timing.

559
00:38:15,744 --> 00:38:16,975
Is Ye Rang in there?

560
00:38:16,975 --> 00:38:19,917
She is, but... that's not the point.

561
00:38:19,917 --> 00:38:21,125
What?

562
00:38:21,776 --> 00:38:23,809
- Come with me.
- Why?

563
00:38:24,805 --> 00:38:26,343
Hyeong Won got it?

564
00:38:26,343 --> 00:38:28,342
That crazy bastard.

565
00:38:28,342 --> 00:38:31,095
It's like he keeps taking Woo Jae's place.

566
00:38:31,095 --> 00:38:33,347
Why does he keep getting tangled up with us?

567
00:38:33,347 --> 00:38:35,100
I know.

568
00:38:35,100 --> 00:38:37,602
Let's find another way.

569
00:38:37,602 --> 00:38:40,527
When did Ye Rang start her agency?

570
00:38:40,527 --> 00:38:42,773
Not for a few more years.

571
00:38:42,773 --> 00:38:44,214
Right.

572
00:38:44,817 --> 00:38:48,154
I'm worried about the camcorder too.

573
00:38:48,154 --> 00:38:49,488
The camcorder?

574
00:38:49,488 --> 00:38:51,908
Carrying it around in my bag isn't safe either.

575
00:38:51,908 --> 00:38:54,493
Bi Gyeong almost broke it just now.

576
00:38:54,493 --> 00:38:55,842
What?

577
00:38:56,562 --> 00:38:59,123
But we can't leave it at home either.

578
00:38:59,123 --> 00:39:00,908
Exactly.

579
00:39:01,751 --> 00:39:04,045
I'm so scared.

580
00:39:04,045 --> 00:39:07,953
What if we suddenly get thrown
into another future again?

581
00:39:07,953 --> 00:39:11,815
What if we can't see Woo Jae again?

582
00:39:12,970 --> 00:39:14,180
No.

583
00:39:14,180 --> 00:39:16,974
As long as we don't drop it, it should be okay.

584
00:39:16,974 --> 00:39:20,127
We know for sure how to get back
to the past where Woo Jae is.

585
00:39:20,127 --> 00:39:22,637
But it's random.

586
00:39:23,519 --> 00:39:26,711
It never goes the way we expect.

587
00:39:36,619 --> 00:39:37,954
<i>I wanted it more.</i>

588
00:39:37,954 --> 00:39:40,747
<i>More than you did.</i>

589
00:39:40,747 --> 00:39:44,929
<i>Turns out, it wasn't just the medal
that I wanted to take from you.</i>

590
00:39:47,171 --> 00:39:50,290
Then that bastard Hyeong Won and Ha Na...

591
00:40:05,815 --> 00:40:08,877
<i>Woo Jae, want to get chicken and beer later?</i>

592
00:40:08,877 --> 00:40:10,736
<i>I'll bring the beer.</i>

593
00:40:10,736 --> 00:40:12,105
<i>Just us two?</i>

594
00:40:43,993 --> 00:40:45,504
<i>I'll pick you up later.</i>

595
00:40:45,504 --> 00:40:47,216
<i>What time do you get off?</i>

596
00:40:51,610 --> 00:40:53,262
- Excuse me.
- Yeah?

597
00:40:53,262 --> 00:40:56,074
Thanks for earlier.

598
00:40:56,790 --> 00:40:58,331
For what?

599
00:40:58,331 --> 00:40:59,995
You weren't saying what needed to be said,

600
00:40:59,995 --> 00:41:02,705
so I couldn't help saying it for you.

601
00:41:02,705 --> 00:41:05,978
Speak up for yourself.
Bottling it up will make you sick.

602
00:41:06,834 --> 00:41:08,654
Thank you.

603
00:41:10,767 --> 00:41:14,717
Jun Mo surprised me, though.

604
00:41:14,717 --> 00:41:17,636
I thought he'd pick Woo Jae for sure.

605
00:41:17,636 --> 00:41:21,640
I didn't think Jun Mo would get swayed by buzz.

606
00:41:21,640 --> 00:41:24,310
Maybe Professor Min got in his head.

607
00:41:24,310 --> 00:41:27,980
That's not the Jun Mo I know.

608
00:41:27,980 --> 00:41:31,192
We should respect Jun Mo's choice.

609
00:41:31,192 --> 00:41:33,912
I'm sure he had his reasons.

610
00:41:35,404 --> 00:41:37,386
But you...

611
00:41:37,386 --> 00:41:39,620
Are you dating Jung Woo Jae?

612
00:41:40,242 --> 00:41:41,911
How did you know?

613
00:41:41,911 --> 00:41:43,954
A college romance

614
00:41:43,954 --> 00:41:47,146
could give you something
to draw on as an actress.

615
00:41:47,146 --> 00:41:49,141
Most couples in their twenties break up anyway.

616
00:41:49,141 --> 00:41:50,319
You won't marry him.

617
00:41:50,319 --> 00:41:53,380
And there's nothing to gain
from making it so obvious.

618
00:41:53,380 --> 00:41:55,763
- Sorry?
- I'm not saying don't date.

619
00:41:55,763 --> 00:41:58,725
I'm saying don't leave behind stuff
you'll regret as an actress.

620
00:41:58,725 --> 00:42:02,272
Like plastering couple photos
all over social media.

621
00:42:02,272 --> 00:42:03,815
<i>What is with her?</i>

622
00:42:03,815 --> 00:42:08,183
<i>Did she already have
this much CEO energy back then?</i>

623
00:42:09,438 --> 00:42:11,482
It's your call, though...

624
00:42:11,482 --> 00:42:15,206
- Just a little advice...
- Thank you so much.

625
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:17,695
Sure.

626
00:42:25,908 --> 00:42:27,589
<i>That was rough, but fun.</i>

627
00:42:27,589 --> 00:42:29,508
<i>- Great work, everyone!
- Great work.</i>

628
00:42:29,508 --> 00:42:31,216
<i>Let's drink!</i>

629
00:42:32,336 --> 00:42:34,569
<i>She's a real star.</i>

630
00:42:34,569 --> 00:42:35,840
<i>Hey, she can't drink.</i>

631
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:38,333
<i>Jun Mo, let's get some air.
The director can't get drunk.</i>

632
00:42:38,333 --> 00:42:39,613
<i>- Shall we get some air?
- Let's go.</i>

633
00:42:39,613 --> 00:42:40,780
<i>Yeah.</i>

634
00:42:41,406 --> 00:42:43,764
<i>Want some ice cream? My treat.</i>

635
00:42:43,764 --> 00:42:45,054
<i>- Really?
- Yeah.</i>

636
00:42:45,054 --> 00:42:46,168
<i>What about Ha Na?</i>

637
00:42:46,168 --> 00:42:47,387
<i>Okay.</i>

638
00:42:57,278 --> 00:42:58,976
<i>Hey!</i>

639
00:42:58,976 --> 00:43:00,359
<i>Yes?</i>

640
00:43:00,359 --> 00:43:01,957
<i>Drink with me.</i>

641
00:43:01,957 --> 00:43:05,418
<i>Ye Rang, so that's what it was.</i>

642
00:43:05,418 --> 00:43:08,005
<i>That's why...</i>

643
00:43:08,005 --> 00:43:10,215
<i>You were so good,</i>

644
00:43:10,215 --> 00:43:14,170
<i>and no matter how hard I practiced,
I couldn't catch up.</i>

645
00:43:14,170 --> 00:43:17,089
<i>I was so jealous of you,</i>

646
00:43:17,089 --> 00:43:20,593
<i>and I hated myself!</i>

647
00:43:20,593 --> 00:43:24,344
<i>I thought you...</i>

648
00:43:24,344 --> 00:43:27,641
<i>hated me for no reason.</i>

649
00:43:27,641 --> 00:43:29,270
<i>Hey...</i>

650
00:43:30,769 --> 00:43:33,272
<i>How could I hate you?</i>

651
00:43:33,272 --> 00:43:35,699
<i>You're this pretty and talented.</i>

652
00:43:35,699 --> 00:43:38,744
<i>Why would I hate you?</i>

653
00:43:38,744 --> 00:43:41,155
<i>Ye Rang, don't cry.</i>

654
00:43:41,155 --> 00:43:43,568
<i>You're pretty too.</i>

655
00:43:44,333 --> 00:43:46,535
<i>No, no.</i>

656
00:43:46,535 --> 00:43:49,580
<i>You're way prettier.</i>

657
00:43:49,580 --> 00:43:53,584
<i>No, you're way prettier.</i>

658
00:43:53,584 --> 00:43:56,128
<i>Come here, little sis.</i>

659
00:43:56,128 --> 00:43:57,692
<i>Ye Rang.</i>

660
00:44:01,973 --> 00:44:04,979
<i>- Don't be silly.
- Don't cry.</i>

661
00:44:11,503 --> 00:44:13,045
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

662
00:44:13,045 --> 00:44:16,440
<i>I'm more sorry, dear.</i>

663
00:44:16,440 --> 00:44:20,517
<i>Back then, I thought she was just this scary,
tough-as-nails senior.</i>

664
00:44:20,517 --> 00:44:23,239
<i>Who knew she had this cute side
hidden underneath?</i>

665
00:44:23,239 --> 00:44:26,005
<i>Should I make the first move this time?</i>

666
00:44:34,922 --> 00:44:36,649
Well...

667
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:39,972
Can I call you "unnie?"

668
00:44:40,654 --> 00:44:41,481
Sorry?

669
00:44:41,481 --> 00:44:44,802
I just think you're so pretty, unnie.

670
00:44:44,802 --> 00:44:46,247
Okay, unnie?

671
00:44:47,810 --> 00:44:51,267
Sure. Whatever you want.

672
00:44:51,267 --> 00:44:52,909
Oh, right.

673
00:44:52,909 --> 00:44:56,355
Someone asked me to give you this.

674
00:44:56,355 --> 00:44:57,445
Who?

675
00:44:57,445 --> 00:45:01,272
My parents' son.

676
00:45:01,926 --> 00:45:03,362
"Your parents' son?"

677
00:45:03,362 --> 00:45:04,498
My brother.

678
00:45:04,498 --> 00:45:05,739
I think he likes you.

679
00:45:05,739 --> 00:45:07,713
He made it himself. Dujjonku.

680
00:45:07,713 --> 00:45:09,941
"Dujjonku?"

681
00:45:10,942 --> 00:45:12,448
Dujjonku...

682
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:21,021
<i>It was nice seeing you this morning, Boss.</i>

683
00:45:21,021 --> 00:45:22,431
<i>This is my number.</i>

684
00:45:22,431 --> 00:45:26,567
<i>If the Dujjonku is good, text "1."
If not, text "2."</i>

685
00:45:26,567 --> 00:45:28,137
What is this?

686
00:45:28,137 --> 00:45:29,822
See you tomorrow.

687
00:45:29,822 --> 00:45:31,609
Oh, okay.

688
00:45:35,388 --> 00:45:37,482
How am I supposed to eat this...

689
00:45:38,605 --> 00:45:40,206
Dujjonku...

690
00:45:41,283 --> 00:45:42,562
<i>Give me your number!</i>

691
00:45:42,562 --> 00:45:45,446
<i>Then that total nutcase from this morning...</i>

692
00:45:45,446 --> 00:45:46,983
Yoon Ha Ru?

693
00:45:57,915 --> 00:45:59,615
[You got a heart]
[Check it out now on Jennypang]

694
00:46:01,374 --> 00:46:04,058
What the heck...

695
00:46:16,560 --> 00:46:18,314
Is it over?

696
00:46:19,521 --> 00:46:21,148
Yeah.

697
00:46:21,148 --> 00:46:24,528
It's really over, right?

698
00:46:26,070 --> 00:46:28,343
No one can find us now.

699
00:46:32,376 --> 00:46:34,203
Just one more time.

700
00:46:36,413 --> 00:46:38,499
Let's call it a day.

701
00:46:38,499 --> 00:46:40,646
We can pick this up tomorrow.

702
00:46:51,762 --> 00:46:54,264
I have training tomorrow.

703
00:46:54,264 --> 00:46:56,809
Shouldn't we do more tonight?

704
00:46:56,809 --> 00:46:59,128
I admire the enthusiasm.

705
00:46:59,128 --> 00:47:01,647
But mindless repetition isn't the answer.

706
00:47:01,647 --> 00:47:05,067
Right now, instead of getting
the lines out of your mouth,

707
00:47:05,067 --> 00:47:08,662
you need time to read the script over and over.

708
00:47:08,662 --> 00:47:09,738
Keep your lips closed.

709
00:47:09,738 --> 00:47:11,995
Read it. Feel it. Think about it.

710
00:47:11,995 --> 00:47:13,826
Really put yourself in Gang Ho's shoes.

711
00:47:13,826 --> 00:47:16,120
You just don't want to practice with me,
do you?

712
00:47:16,120 --> 00:47:19,048
I'm just saying, use your enthusiasm...

713
00:47:20,628 --> 00:47:22,793
Ye Rang texted me a "1!"

714
00:47:22,793 --> 00:47:24,128
Look! "1!"

715
00:47:24,128 --> 00:47:25,795
See?

716
00:47:26,380 --> 00:47:27,897
Hey! See this?

717
00:47:27,897 --> 00:47:29,057
"1!"

718
00:47:29,057 --> 00:47:30,283
So proud of myself.

719
00:47:30,283 --> 00:47:33,176
See? She sent me a "1!"

720
00:47:34,248 --> 00:47:36,139
Oh, this...

721
00:47:39,551 --> 00:47:41,100
By the way...

722
00:47:41,728 --> 00:47:43,724
What are you doing here?

723
00:47:55,834 --> 00:47:58,328
Come here.

724
00:47:58,328 --> 00:47:59,438
Are you crazy?

725
00:47:59,438 --> 00:48:02,532
What? Just come here.

726
00:48:03,125 --> 00:48:04,501
Let go.

727
00:48:04,501 --> 00:48:06,931
Come on, you bastard.

728
00:48:15,429 --> 00:48:17,245
Want some chicken?

729
00:48:17,245 --> 00:48:18,556
Let's eat.

730
00:48:19,770 --> 00:48:21,214
I'll open it for you.

731
00:48:26,703 --> 00:48:28,358
Is judo a joke to you?

732
00:48:28,358 --> 00:48:30,370
You think your spot is secure?

733
00:48:35,624 --> 00:48:38,619
When Woo Jae got hurt
and you made the national team,

734
00:48:38,619 --> 00:48:42,147
everyone ran their mouth
about how you got lucky, right?

735
00:48:42,748 --> 00:48:44,032
Of course.

736
00:48:44,032 --> 00:48:45,959
Just loudmouths talking crap.

737
00:48:45,959 --> 00:48:48,170
But I know.

738
00:48:48,170 --> 00:48:49,588
Judo doesn't lie.

739
00:48:49,588 --> 00:48:50,672
It wasn't luck.

740
00:48:50,672 --> 00:48:53,509
All that time on the mat
got you on the national team.

741
00:48:53,509 --> 00:48:56,099
Sweat on the mat never betrays you.

742
00:48:56,099 --> 00:48:58,639
You're the one doing the betraying.

743
00:48:58,639 --> 00:49:00,098
Think carefully.

744
00:49:00,098 --> 00:49:01,475
About what you really want.

745
00:49:01,475 --> 00:49:04,167
Where you really belong.

746
00:49:06,480 --> 00:49:08,631
Don't cross the line.

747
00:49:08,631 --> 00:49:11,151
You could seriously get yourself killed.

748
00:49:11,151 --> 00:49:14,446
What's with that death glare?

749
00:49:14,446 --> 00:49:15,995
Who are you threatening?

750
00:49:15,995 --> 00:49:20,371
I'm only saying this
because I want you to do well...

751
00:49:26,813 --> 00:49:29,799
That temper of his...

752
00:49:30,504 --> 00:49:32,295
Seriously...

753
00:49:32,295 --> 00:49:34,010
Beats me.

754
00:49:34,748 --> 00:49:36,900
Darn it!

755
00:49:54,072 --> 00:49:55,398
[Coach Jang]

756
00:50:05,855 --> 00:50:08,125
Once you've looked it all over,
give it one final check.

757
00:50:08,125 --> 00:50:09,543
Check the schedule too.

758
00:50:09,543 --> 00:50:11,781
- Yeah.
- In this scene...

759
00:50:16,392 --> 00:50:18,069
I'm Jang Jeong Ho, the judo team coach.

760
00:50:18,069 --> 00:50:20,574
Who's in charge here?

761
00:50:21,271 --> 00:50:23,577
That's me. What is this about?

762
00:50:23,577 --> 00:50:24,766
What is this about?

763
00:50:24,766 --> 00:50:26,768
You have to ask?

764
00:50:26,768 --> 00:50:28,145
Is this about Lee Hyeong Won?

765
00:50:28,145 --> 00:50:29,605
Yes, right.

766
00:50:29,605 --> 00:50:32,024
You know he's on
Korea's national judo team, right?

767
00:50:32,024 --> 00:50:33,170
Yes, I do.

768
00:50:33,170 --> 00:50:35,694
He chose to audition himself,

769
00:50:35,694 --> 00:50:39,831
and I understand the four-day shoot
falls during his official leave.

770
00:50:39,831 --> 00:50:40,832
Ma'am.

771
00:50:40,832 --> 00:50:44,202
We'll be one month out
from an international competition.

772
00:50:44,202 --> 00:50:46,079
He'll be cutting kilos every day

773
00:50:46,079 --> 00:50:50,542
and watching every move
to avoid injury in training.

774
00:50:50,542 --> 00:50:52,836
We also plan to make sure
the shoot doesn't strain him...

775
00:50:52,836 --> 00:50:54,838
Those four days...

776
00:50:54,838 --> 00:50:56,673
could erase ten years of work

777
00:50:56,673 --> 00:50:58,934
and cost Korea a gold medal.

778
00:50:58,934 --> 00:51:01,392
That's what I'm telling you!

779
00:51:01,392 --> 00:51:02,414
Ma'am.

780
00:51:02,414 --> 00:51:05,443
Can you take responsibility for his life?

781
00:51:12,564 --> 00:51:14,339
President?

782
00:51:15,020 --> 00:51:16,674
Professor Min.

783
00:51:17,491 --> 00:51:18,882
Let's keep this short.

784
00:51:18,882 --> 00:51:21,691
Get Lee Hyeong Won back immediately.

785
00:51:31,042 --> 00:51:33,008
I'm truly sorry.

786
00:51:35,477 --> 00:51:37,298
It can't be helped.

787
00:51:55,958 --> 00:51:58,701
Is this all of it?

788
00:51:58,701 --> 00:51:59,820
Yeah.

789
00:51:59,820 --> 00:52:01,780
Sponsors sent it for Hyeong Won.

790
00:52:01,780 --> 00:52:03,281
Now it's a goodbye gift.

791
00:52:03,281 --> 00:52:05,283
They only sent tiny stuff.

792
00:52:05,283 --> 00:52:07,810
You're mad you can't eat it now. Right?

793
00:52:08,412 --> 00:52:10,171
We're about to shoot.

794
00:52:10,171 --> 00:52:12,499
What good is any of this sponsorship stuff now?

795
00:52:12,499 --> 00:52:13,842
That jerk...

796
00:52:13,842 --> 00:52:16,962
His judo matters, but our movie's a joke?

797
00:52:16,962 --> 00:52:18,380
I never liked him either.

798
00:52:18,380 --> 00:52:20,257
He's just so unlikeable.

799
00:52:20,257 --> 00:52:21,892
He wasn't treating it like a joke.

800
00:52:21,892 --> 00:52:23,106
He was serious about it.

801
00:52:23,106 --> 00:52:25,679
That's why he's genuinely sorry.

802
00:52:25,679 --> 00:52:27,814
He must be crushed.

803
00:52:27,814 --> 00:52:30,219
Thinking about how upset Hyeong Won must be

804
00:52:30,219 --> 00:52:32,457
makes me feel even worse.

805
00:52:33,603 --> 00:52:35,354
It was ridiculous from the start.

806
00:52:35,354 --> 00:52:38,817
Casting a national team athlete
right before training camp?

807
00:52:38,817 --> 00:52:42,243
I got blinded by the buzz. My bad.

808
00:52:44,972 --> 00:52:46,207
<i>Wait.</i>

809
00:52:46,207 --> 00:52:49,314
<i>This is sudden, but isn't it actually good?</i>

810
00:52:49,314 --> 00:52:52,494
<i>The guy who swooped in
is out of the picture. Then...</i>

811
00:52:52,494 --> 00:52:54,713
So what are you going to do?

812
00:52:55,709 --> 00:52:57,399
Jung Woo Jae...

813
00:52:57,986 --> 00:53:00,319
Shouldn't we call him before it's too late?

814
00:53:01,650 --> 00:53:03,550
Yeah. Right.

815
00:53:03,550 --> 00:53:05,128
